From: Daniel Schwierzeck <daniel.schwierzeck@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] pinctrl: airoha: fix setting of GPIO direction

GPIO_CTRL allocates two bits per GPIO with values 0x2 and 0x3 reserved.
Patch 111 regressed airoha_gpio_set_direction() to a 1-bit mask, leaving
the upper bit set when switching direction. Always clear both bits via
GENMASK(offset + 1, offset) and set BIT(offset) for output.

Origin: backport from Linux commit 2b99a9d8e8d9 ("pinctrl: airoha: fix setting of GPIO direction")
Signed-off-by: Daniel Schwierzeck <daniel.schwierzeck@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/pinctrl/airoha/pinctrl-airoha.c
+++ b/drivers/pinctrl/airoha/pinctrl-airoha.c
@@ -190,7 +190,7 @@ static int airoha_gpio_set_direction(str
 				     unsigned int gpio, bool input)
 {
 	u32 mask, index;
-	int err;
+	int err, offset;
 
 	/* set output enable */
 	mask = BIT(gpio % AIROHA_PIN_BANK_SIZE);
@@ -202,12 +202,13 @@ static int airoha_gpio_set_direction(str
 		return err;
 
 	/* set direction */
-	mask = BIT(2 * (gpio % AIROHA_REG_GPIOCTRL_NUM_PIN));
+	offset = 2 * (gpio % AIROHA_REG_GPIOCTRL_NUM_PIN);
+	mask = GENMASK(offset + 1, offset); /* 2-bit GPIO_CTRL field; 0x2/0x3 reserved */
 	index = gpio / AIROHA_REG_GPIOCTRL_NUM_PIN;
 
 	return regmap_update_bits(pinctrl->regmap,
 				  pinctrl->gpio_regs->dir[index], mask,
-				  !input ? mask : 0);
+				  !input ? BIT(offset) : 0);
 }
 
 /* pinmux callbacks */
